    fix: AUG-072 fresh-start seed remember no longer 400s on empty seed
    
    Root cause (verified live, not the board row's original guess): the payload is
    NOT missing fields. DuckBrain's POST /api/memories required-content gate
    (DB-GAP-058, duckbrain src/http/routes/memories.ts) 400s content == "" with
    "Missing required fields: key, domain, content" (VALIDATION_ERROR). cmd_start
    called remember(ns, f"/auger/{pid}/seed", seed) UNCONDITIONALLY, and with no
    --seed/--seed-file the seed is "", so every fresh no-seed start printed the 400
    line and exited 1 with the seed note never stored.
    
    Fix: skip the remember call when the seed is empty (`if seed:`). An empty seed
    has nothing to store or embed; skipping is correct behavior. With a non-empty
    seed the path is unchanged (store + embed + both print lines). The project-row
    insert and remember()'s signature are untouched.
    
    RED proof (tests run against HEAD's unfixed cmd_start via `git stash push --
    auger.py`):
    
        tests/test_auger.py::test_start_with_empty_seed_never_calls_remember FAILED
        >       assert calls == [], f"remember was called with an empty seed: {calls}"
        E       AssertionError: remember was called with an empty seed:
        E         [('auger-worker072-unit', '/auger/P-EMPTYSEED/seed', '')]
        1 failed, 1 passed
    
    Test B (with-seed stores/embeds exactly once with key /auger/<pid>/seed) was
    already green on unfixed code, as expected. Both green after the fix.
    
    Live verification against DuckBrain 127.0.0.1:3000:
    - unfixed: `start` on a fresh ns -> the 400 VALIDATION_ERROR line, exit 1.
    - fixed, no seed: exit 0, "project P-... in namespace ...", no 400 text.
    - fixed, --seed "hello seed": exit 0, seed note retrievable via `recall`
      (1.000 /auger/P-.../seed). Both repro namespaces torn down after.
    
    Gate: bash tests/gate.sh -> GATE PASS (syntax, ruff clean, pytest green,
    live smoke 21 passed / 0 failed, 2 live arms ran). ruff check auger.py +
    tests/test_auger.py clean; py_compile clean.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
